   "question": "Which clients are below the RAROC hurdle but have cross-sell whitespace?",
   "answer": "**Headline:** 20 clients are below the 15% RAROC hurdle and each has cross\u2011sell whitespace.\n\n**Drivers**\n- Lakemont Data \u2013 RAROC 12%, revenue $1.9M, missing Debt Capital Markets, Equity Capital Markets, M&A Advisory.  \n- Alder Data \u2013 RAROC 9%, revenue $0.95M, missing Debt Capital Markets, Equity Capital Markets, M&A Advisory, Rates & FX Hedging, Transaction Banking.  \n- Hollins Energy \u2013 RAROC 9%, revenue $0.65M, missing Debt Capital Markets, Equity Capital Markets, M&A Advisory, Rates & FX Hedging, Transaction Banking.  \n- Queensway Capital \u2013 RAROC 5%, revenue $1.2M, missing Debt Capital Markets, Equity Capital Markets, Lending, M&A Advisory, Rates & FX Hedging.  \n- Northwind Midstream \u2013 RAROC 6%, revenue $0.86M, missing Debt Capital Markets, Equity Capital Markets, M&A Advisory, Rates & FX Hedging, Transaction Banking.\n\n**Executive paragraph**  \nAll 20 clients in the latest view fall short of the 15% hurdle and have at least one product gap. The cohort is split 19 Mid\u2011Market and 1 Financial Institutions client. Eighteen hold only Lending, one holds Transaction Banking, and one holds Lending, Rates & FX Hedging, and Transaction Banking. The lowest\u2011RAROC client is Queensway Capital (5%) which is missing five fee\u2011product opportunities.\n\n**Definitions used**\n- RAROC: Risk\u2011adjusted return on capital, measured over the trailing 12 months as a percentage. (Source: CIB Business Definitions Glossary \u203a RAROC)  \n- Hurdle rate: The minimum RAROC required (15%); gap to hurdle = RAROC\u202f\u2212\u202f15%. (Source: CIB Business Definitions Glossary \u203a Hurdle rate)  \n- Cross\u2011sell whitespace: Products a below\u2011hurdle client does not yet hold; missing products are those not generating revenue in the trailing 12 months. (Source: CIB Business Definitions Glossary \u203a Cross\u2011sell whitespace)\n\n_Synthetic data \u00b7 Northlake Bank (fictional). Data as of 2026-11-24._",
