   "answer": "**Headline:** Coverage\u202fEast\u202f2 is the only team over capacity; its win rate is falling every quarter.\n\n**Drivers**\n- Over\u2011capacity flag: true (clients per banker\u202f14\u202fvs target\u202f10)  \n- Win\u2011rate trend: \u201cfalling every quarter\u201d  \n- Win\u2011rate Q4\u202f2025: 44%  \n- Win\u2011rate Q3\u202f2026: 25% (0.25)\n\n**Executive paragraph**  \nCoverage\u202fEast\u202f2 exceeds its client\u2011per\u2011banker target, indicating bankers are stretched thin. The team\u2019s win rate has declined each quarter from 44% to 25%, consistent with the expected impact of over\u2011capacity on deal success.\n\n**Definitions used**\n- Coverage capacity: How many client relationships each coverage banker carries compared with the team\u2019s target; over capacity when clients per banker\u202f>\u202ftarget (Source: CIB Business Definitions Glossary \u203a Coverage capacity)  \n- Win rate: Share of decided deals that Northlake won; win rate\u202f=\u202fdeals won\u202f\u00f7\u202f(deals won\u202f+\u202fdeals lost) (Source: CIB Business Definitions Glossary \u203a Win rate)\n\n_Synthetic data \u00b7 Northlake Bank (fictional). Data as of 2026-11-24._",
