   "question": "Are there any reconciliation breaks?",
   "answer": "**Headline:** Yes \u2013 a $1.2\u202fM reconciliation break was identified for Transaction Banking in June\u202f2026.  \n\n**Drivers**\n- Product\u202fTransaction Banking (P06) \u2013 GL $12.4\u202fM vs booked $11.2\u202fM, delta $1.2\u202fM.  \n- Month\u202f2026\u201106 \u2013 delta exceeds the $1\u202fK tolerance.  \n- Period\u202f2024\u201110\u201101 to 2026\u201111\u201124 \u2013 145 months checked.  \n- Severity\u202f1 \u2013 break \u2265\u202f$1\u202fM (per SOP).  \n\n**Executive paragraph**  \nThe reconciliation control flagged a break for Transaction Banking in June\u202f2026, with the GL control total $12.4\u202fM exceeding booked revenue by $1.2\u202fM. The size places the issue in Severity\u202f1, requiring escalation to the Head of CIB Finance within two business days and tracking on the CFO office watch list if not resolved by the second month\u2011end.  \n\n**Definitions used**\n- Reconciliation break: A product and month where booked revenue differs from the GL control total by more than $1,000; positive delta indicates a missing booking. (Source: CIB Business Definitions Glossary)  \n- Severity\u202f1: A reconciliation break of $1\u202fM or more, or any break open at a second month\u2011end. (Source: SOP: Data-Quality (DQ) and Reconciliation Breaks)  \n- Escalation (Severity\u202f1): Head of CIB Finance notified within two business days; unresolved after two further month\u2011ends escalates to the CFO office watch list. (Source: SOP: Data-Quality (DQ) and Reconciliation Breaks)\n\n_Synthetic data \u00b7 Northlake Bank (fictional). Data as of 2026-11-24._",
